PRIVACY POLICY

PDF Editor: Fill & Sign Forms

Last updated: June 5, 2026
Effective date: June 5, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how [YOUR NAME / COMPANY NAME] ("we," "us," or "our")
handles information in connection with the mobile application "PDF Editor: Fill &
Sign Forms" (Android package name: com.nageshwarrao.pdfstudio) (the "App"). By
downloading or using the App, you agree to this Privacy Policy.

1. OUR PRIVACY-FIRST APPROACH
The App is designed to work offline and to keep your documents on your device. We
do not require you to create an account, and we do not sell or rent your personal
information. The App does not upload your PDF files to any server.

2. INFORMATION WE COLLECT
a) Information you provide. The App does not ask you to register or to provide
personal information such as your name, email address, or phone number.

b) Your documents and content. PDFs and files you open, create, edit, fill, sign,
or save are processed entirely on your device and stored in the App's private
storage. We do not access, transmit, collect, or store your documents.

c) Information we collect automatically. The App does not contain our own
analytics or tracking tools and does not collect usage data, device identifiers,
or location for our own use.

d) Information collected through advertising. The App may display advertisements
provided by third-party advertising networks (for example, Google AdMob). When
ads are enabled, these networks may automatically collect certain information
through their own software, such as your device's advertising identifier
(Advertising ID), IP address, general device information, and app interaction or
diagnostic data, in accordance with their own privacy policies, to deliver and
measure advertising. If the version of the App you are using does not display
ads, no such information is collected.

3. PERMISSIONS
The App is built to request as few permissions as possible. It does not request
access to your contacts, camera, microphone, precise location, or broad
file/storage access. To open or save a PDF, the App uses Android's built-in
document picker (Storage Access Framework), which lets you choose individual
files without granting the App access to your entire device storage. When
advertising is enabled, the App uses the Internet permission to load ads.

4. ADVERTISING
We may use third-party advertising networks, such as Google AdMob, to show ads
in the App. These third parties may use cookies, device identifiers (including
the Advertising ID), and similar technologies to collect the information
described above and to serve personalized or non-personalized ads.

We do not control the data practices of these advertising networks. To learn how
Google uses data from apps that use its advertising services, see:
https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

You can limit ad personalization or reset your Advertising ID at any time in your
device settings (on Android: Settings > Privacy or Google > Ads).

For users in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, Switzerland,
and other regions where required, the App will ask for your consent before
serving personalized ads, using a consent mechanism such as Google's User
Messaging Platform.

5. HOW INFORMATION IS USED
Information collected by advertising partners is used to display and measure ads
and to control how often you see a particular ad. We do not use your documents
for advertising or for any purpose other than providing the App's features to you.

6. DATA SHARING
We do not sell your personal information and we do not share your documents with
anyone. The only data shared is the limited information collected by our
advertising partners when ads are enabled (as described above), and any content
you choose to share yourself using the App's Share or Print features, which you
direct to apps and services of your own choosing.

7. DATA SECURITY
Your files are stored in the App's private, sandboxed storage on your device.
Because your documents remain on your device, their security also depends on your
device's own protections (such as a lock screen and device encryption).

8. DATA RETENTION AND DELETION
Your documents remain on your device until you delete them within the App or
uninstall the App. Uninstalling the App removes the documents stored in its
private storage. We do not keep copies of your files.

9. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY
The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your
country), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If
advertising is enabled, ads will be handled in a manner consistent with
applicable laws (such as COPPA) and Google Play's Families policy, and
personalized ads will not be served to users identified as children.

10. YOUR RIGHTS AND CHOICES
Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal
information (for example, under the GDPR or the CCPA/CPRA). Because we do not
collect personal information ourselves, requests relating to advertising data
should also be directed to the relevant advertising network. You can control ad
personalization through your device settings as described above, and you may
contact us using the details below.

11. INTERNATIONAL USERS
The App can be used worldwide. Any limited data processed by advertising partners
may be processed in countries other than your own, subject to those partners'
policies and safeguards.

12. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise
the "Last updated" date above. Material changes (such as enabling advertising)
will be reflected here. Your continued use of the App after changes take effect
constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.


